          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong rational topological space
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            all whose (reduced)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral homology
            groups are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            and passing to that rationalization amounts to forgetting all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+groups"} homology
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy
          %p
            Thereby rational spaces serve as approximations to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p The idea is that comparatively little information (though sometimes crucial information) is lost by passing to rationalizations, while there are powerful tools to handle and compute with rational spaces.
          %p
            In particular, there is a precise sense in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+space"}> nilpotent
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            = succeed ":" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                differential graded cochain algebras
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/differential+graded+cochain+algebras"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is called
            %em rational
            if
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                it is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
                in that the 1st
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                vanishes,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 X = 0
                (more generally we may use
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+topological+spaces"} nilpotent topological spaces
                here)
            %li
              %p and the following equivalent conditions are satisfied
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the collection of
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℚ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"} reduced homology
                    of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi H
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_*(X,\mathbb{Z})
                    is a
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℚ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology"} reduced homology
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
                    of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi H
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_*(\Omega X,\mathbb{Z})
                    is a
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℚ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          %p
            A morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell : X \to Y
            of simply connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is called a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a rational topological space and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            in rational homology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_*(\ell,\mathbb{Q}) : H_*(X,\mathbb{Q}) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_*(Y,\mathbb{Q})
                  \\,.
          %p
            Equivlently,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
            is a rationalization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            if it induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            on the rationalized
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi ℓ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_* \ell \otimes \mathbb{Q} : \pi_* X \otimes \mathbb{Q}
                  \\to \pi_* Y \otimes \mathbb{Q} \simeq \pi_* Y
          %p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            A continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Y
            between simply connected space is a
            %strong rational homotopy equivalence
            if the following equivalent conditions are satisfied:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                it induces an isomorphism on rationalized homotopy groups in that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_*(\phi) \otimes \mathbb{Q}
                is an isomorphism;
            %li
              %p
                it induces an isomorphism on rationalized homology groups in that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_*(\phi,\mathbb{Q})
                is an isomorohism;
            %li
              %p
                it induces an isomorphism on rationalized
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^*(\phi,\mathbb{Q})
                is an isomorphism;
            %li
              %p
                it induces a weak
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                on rationalizations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0, Y_0
                in that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_0 : X_0 \to Y_0
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            One of the central theorems of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            says:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Rational homotopy types of simply connected spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are in bijective corespondence with minimal
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V,d)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Sullivan
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\wedge^\bullet V , d) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{Sullivan}(X)
                    \\,.
            %p And homotopy classes of morphisms on both sides are in bijection.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p This appears for instance as corollary 1.26 in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                ,
                %em Rational homotopy theory: a brief introduction
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0604626"}> arXiv
                )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#rational_sphere
            Rational
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+n-sphere"} rational n-sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S^n)_0
            can be written as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∨
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo )
                  %mo ∪
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                    %msubsup
                      %mi D
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (S^n)_0  :=
                  \\left(
                  \\vee_{k\geq 1} S^n_k
                  \\right)
                  \\cup
                  \\left(
                  \\coprod_{k \geq 2} D^{n+1}_k
                  \\right)
                  \\,,
          %p where…
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2 k +1
            odd, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            for the
            = succeed "-sphere" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            with a single generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and vanishing differential, i.e. the morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi Sullivan
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\wedge^\bullet \langle c\rangle, d = 0)
                  \\to
                  \\Omega^\bullet_{Sullivan}(S^{2k + 1})
          %p
            that picks any representative of the degree
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2k
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 1
            there is a second generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_{4k+1}
            with differential
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d c_{2k} = 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d c_{4k-1} = c_{2k} \wedge c_{2k}
                  \\,.
          %h3#rational_disk
            Rational
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The rational
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            of the rational sphere:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi D
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi S
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D^{n+1}_{\mathbb{Q}} = C(S^n_{\mathbb{Q}}) = (S^n_{\mathbb{Q}}\times I)/(S^n_{\mathbb{Q}}\times\{0\}).
          %p
            Since the cochain complex of the
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d} b = c
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cdga"} cdga
            corresponding to the rational
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b^k
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c b^k
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is even, with differentials:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi k
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d}(b^k)
                  \\;=\;
                  k \cdot c b^{k-1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d} (c b^k)
                  \\;=\;
                  0
                  \\,,
          %p
            and of linear combinations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mi k
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^k b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^k
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is odd, with differentials
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mi k
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d}(c^k b)=c^{k+1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d(c^k)=0
                  \\,.
          %h3#rational_compact_liegroups Rational compact Lie-groups
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi rank
                      %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\mu_{k_i}\}_{i=1}^{rank G}
            be generators of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg \mu_{k_i} = 2 k_i-1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{P_{k_i}\}_i
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            Such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is rationally equivalent to the product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi rank
                      %mi G
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\prod_{i = 1}^{rank G} S^{2 k_i -1}
          %p
            of rational
            = succeed "-spheres." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Moreover, Lie groups are
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+homotopy+type"} formal homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            to its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
          %h3#RationalClassifyingSpace Rational classifying spaces of compact Lie groups
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as above, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            be the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^\bullet(\mathcal{B}G, \mathbb{Q}) \simeq \mathbb{Q}[P_{k_1},  P_{k_2}, \cdots]
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{k_i}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            generator in degre
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 k_i
          %p
            Indeed, also these classifying spaces are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+homotopy+type"} formal homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H^\bullet(\mathcal{B}G,\mathbb{R}), d=0)
          %h3#quotient_spaces Quotient spaces
          %p
            We may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *// G
          %p …
          %h3#biquotient_spaces Biquotient spaces
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi H
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \subset H \times H
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+group"} direct product group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            by left and right multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi h
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mi h
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (g_1, g_2) : h \mapsto g_1 h g_2^{-1}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biquotient"} biquotient
          %p …
          %p See
          %ul
            %li
              Vitali Kapovitch,
              %em A note on rational homotopy of biquotients
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.utoronto.ca/vtk/biquotient.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+G-space"} rational topological G-space
